    "status": "present",
    "value": "Removing bricks splits components, which union-find cannot do, but adding bricks only merges them. So apply every hit first, build components of the remaining bricks with a virtual roof node joined to every top-row brick, and then restore the hits in reverse order. When a brick that existed originally is restored, the bricks that newly become connected to the roof are exactly those that fell when it was hit. The answer for that hit is the growth of the roof component's size minus one (the restored brick itself), floored at 0."
  },
